// A comment inside an import is written before the line, not after it. The
// alias sits past the path's end, so a comment between `as` and it was first
// seen while the line was being ended -- and one seen there is placed after
// the declaration it was written inside, which walks it one declaration down
// every time the file is formatted. Formatting is a normal form, so a shape
// with no fixed point is not a cosmetic complaint.
// between as and the alias
import m as other

use m.A

fn main() -> UInt8 {
    0
}
